   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the highway law, in relation to designating New York state route 375 from the intersection of New York state route 28 in West Hurley to the intersection of New York state route 212 in Woodstock as the \"Levon Helm Memorial Boulevard\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S3935",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3935-2013",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §344-b, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S3935               REVISED 5/16/13\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the highway law, in relation to\ndesignating New York state route 375 from the intersection of New York\nstate route 28 in West Hurley to the intersection of New York state\nroute 212 in Woodstock as the \"Levon Helm Memorial Boulevard\"\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:  To honor the life and music of Mark\nLevon Helm, longtime Woodstock, NY resident and Grammy winning\npercussionist who achieved fame as the drummer and frequent lead and\nbacking vocalist for The Band.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends the Highway Law by adding a new section 344-b which\ndesignates the portion of the highway system on New York State Route\n375 beginning at the intersection of New York State Route 28 in West\nHurley and ending at the intersection of New York State Route 212 in\nWoodstock as the \"Levon Helm Memorial Boulevard\".\n\nSection 2: Requires the Commissioner of the Department of\nTransportation to provide for the installation and maintenance of\nadequate signing of the state highway system as designated pursuant to\nthis act.\n\nSection 3: Effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  This highway will be designated in recognition of\nLevon Helm, Grammy winning artist and longtime Woodstock, New York\nresident. The naming of this highway which runs near Helm's barn where\nhis famous \"Midnight Rambles\" were held and near \"Big Pink,\" the home\nwhere The Band produced their award winning album by the same name,\nwill honor Helm's memory while distinguishing that the Woodstock area\nhad a significant impact on his life.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY: New bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:  The cost of proper signage along the route which\nis expected to cost between $3,000 and $4,000.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:  This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
